# Printventory - 3D Model Manager

Printventory is a desktop application for managing 3D printing model collections. It provides a comprehensive set of features for organizing, viewing, and managing 3D model files.

## Core Features

### File Management
- Scan directories for STL and 3MF files (up to 50MB per file)
- View thumbnails of 3D models in a responsive grid layout
- Sort models by name, size, or date
- Quick access to file location
- Delete files with database cleanup
- Backup and restore database
- Virtual grid rendering for performance optimization

### Model Organization
- Tag models for easy categorization
- Assign designers to models
- Track print status (printed/not printed)
- Add source URLs and notes
- Link related models (parent/child relationships)
- Assign licenses to models

### Multi-Edit Features
- Select multiple models for batch editing
- Bulk update designer, source, print status, and parent model
- Select all visible models with one click
- Filter models by various attributes

### Duplicate Management
- Find duplicate files based on content hash
- Compare duplicates with thumbnails
- Easily remove duplicate files

### Interface Features
- Customizable model background color
- Context menu for quick actions
- Responsive grid layout
- Real-time search and filtering
- Tag management system
- Auto-save changes

### Data Management
- Database backup and restore
- Purge all model data option
- Automatic thumbnail generation
- Preserve metadata during rescans

### AI Integration
- AI-powered automatic tagging of models
- Integration with OpenAI and other AI services
- Configurable AI settings

### Slicer Integration
- Open models directly in configured slicers
- Support for multiple slicer applications
- Customizable slicer paths

## Technical Architecture

### Frontend
- Electron-based desktop application
- HTML/CSS/JavaScript UI
- Three.js for 3D model rendering
- Virtual scrolling for performance optimization

### Backend
- Node.js
- SQLite database (better-sqlite3)
- File system operations for model management
- Thumbnail generation

### Database Schema
- models: Stores model metadata (filepath, filename, size, etc.)
- tags: Stores available tags
- model_tags: Maps tags to models
- settings: Application settings
- slicers: Configured slicer applications

